>> Hi John,
>> On 2026-04-09 at 17:37:22 -0700, John Harrison wrote:
>>> On 3/23/26 21:27, Kandpal, Suraj wrote:
>>>> Currently I am seeing some alignment issues when running the tool.
>>>>
>>> I don't know what you mean by this? Alignment of the info text on the
>>> screen?
> So if there was a gitlab I could share the photo but it seems that the status end up getting overlapped with content TYPE info.
I looks fine to me, see attached. What screen size are you running at? 
I'm running on a 1920x1080 panel.

The code seems to use a lot of magic numbers in the determine the 
positions for the text rendering (width - 20, height - 60, etc.). My 
patch didn't add any of those, I just re-used the existing calculations. 
Hmm, it is also confused as to the vertical position of the text. One 
calculation is assuming the text is drawn above the cursor position 
(correct) and another seems to assume it is drawn below (incorrect)!

The font size is based on the detected screen size (font_size = 
data->height / 12.0). So I guess those magic numbers were chosen against 
a specific screen size and are incorrect for smaller resolutions. Sounds 
like it needs an extra patch to replace all the magic numbers with 
multiples of the font size. Otherwise, no matter where you put the text, 
you are going to hit issues with some unexpected resolution.

John.

